[[File:Echo boots detail.png|150px|left]]
'''Echo boots''' are an enhanced pair of [[guardian boots]] which require level 75 [[Defence]] to wear. They are made by combining the boots with an [[echo crystal]], a rare drop from participating in the [[Fortis Colosseum]]. Compared to its predecessor, it gives an additional +2 [[prayer bonus]] and a passive effect in which the boots deal 1 recoil damage to any target that damages the player, limited to a 3x3 square centered on the player. This effectively restricts recoiled targets to only those in melee range.

Each echo crystal will add 6,000 charges to the recoil effect (costing {{Coins|{{GEP|Echo crystal}}/6000}} per charge), up to a maximum of 60,000. The recoil effect can be toggled via the boots' "Toggle-activity" option, allowing players to disable it as to not waste it during casual training, and instead use it in activities where the effect may prove more useful. The "Revert" option reverts the echo boots back into guardian boots, though this '''will not''' return any echo crystals, regardless of whether or not any recoil charges were used. Players can configure the charges while the boots are in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials.

Like the Bandos and guardian boots used in their creation, they will render followers of [[Bandos]] [[unaggressive]] to the wearer in the [[God Wars Dungeon]].

